Durable logical sessions (V6/V11 stage A): /save, /sessions, /resume. Portable text only; no cache is serialized.

Closed test debt first
- tests/server_reuse.rs: a real `marin serve` of the tiny chat model with a 2048 window (config patched to 8192
  positions, tests/common/long.rs) is used by `marin code` ("using the Marin server on port 8000 (gamma)", answer from
  the server's 2048 window); the earlier rejection cases (other model, 1024 window, silent / dripping / non-JSON
  impostors) still pass.
- tests/modes_long.rs (piped) and tests/modes_long_pty.rs (real terminal) on that long-window model: a chat question
  does not reach the code prompt, /clear forgets only the current mode, code history survives a trip to chat, model
  switching starts both over, Ctrl-C in code mode prints "cancelled; that question was not kept" and the prompt works.
- tests/chat_reuse.rs: with MARIN_QWEN35_Q8_DIR (required when MARIN_REQUIRE_CUDA is set) a Qwen3.5 CUDA question
  cancelled while its prompt is read leaves a cache whose next answer equals a full replay's, with the conversation
  before it still reused.
- Behavior change found by the persistence rule: a chat reply stopped with Ctrl-C used to stay in the conversation
  (partial text). It is now dropped like a failed question and like code mode, so live and saved conversations agree.

Session store (crates/cli/src/saved/)
- Format `marin-session` version 1, JSON: name, saved_at, model {name, hash of config+tokenizer files}, mode, chat
  items, optional code {root, items}. Items are the existing code::Item (User / Assistant / Results{done,note,elided}).
- Folder `<state>/sessions` mode 700 (made by Marin; a looser or linked folder is refused), files mode 600 written
  under a hidden temporary name, fsynced, renamed into place, directory fsynced. Temporary files older than 10 min are
  removed by the next save. Names are [A-Za-z0-9._-], at most 64, not starting with . or -. Files at most 2 MiB, at most
  100 sessions. An existing file is replaced only if it is itself a valid session; links are never followed.
- Refused with the reason, nothing changed: truncated / non-JSON / foreign JSON, version other than 1, oversized,
  name that disagrees with the file name, half exchanges, other model name, changed config or tokenizer, missing
  project folder, window too small for code mode.

Results (tests: crates/cli/src/saved/tests.rs, crates/cli/tests/sessions.rs, modes_long_pty.rs)
- Save -> new process -> resume -> save: identical chat and code history. A resumed chat continues exactly as the
  uninterrupted conversation (tiny model CPU, temperature 0; Qwen3.5-4B-Q8 CUDA, 3 turns, identical history).
- Process killed with SIGKILL while saving in a loop (8 delays, 4000 saves queued): the session file always parsed and
  held the full exchange; only a stale temporary file can remain.
- SIGINT during a chat answer and during a code answer: `/save` afterwards says "nothing to save yet" and no file exists.
- Damaged, truncated, newer-version, 3 MiB, foreign and non-session files are listed as damaged or refused by name.
- Real code session on Qwen3.5-4B-Q8 CUDA (3 tool calls): saved, resumed from another directory in a new process, and
  the follow-up "what file did you read?" was answered from the restored tool history.

Cost (Qwen3-0.6B CPU, Qwen3.5-4B-Q8 CUDA; 4 runs each, `hello` and one short question, same machine)
  qwen3-0.6b cpu        HEAD wall median 3.35 s  new 3.19 s   peak RSS 1312.7 / 1313.0 MiB
  qwen3.5-4b-q8 cuda    HEAD wall median 5.79 s  new 5.72 s   peak RSS  871.4 /  871.1 MiB
  peak VRAM (nvidia-smi, 0.2 s samples) 5216 MiB for both. Nothing is read or written at startup.
Not verified: ownership of an existing sessions folder (only its mode and type are checked); concurrent saves of one
name from two processes (the last rename wins, each file is whole).
